Xenophon 1: The Blade Of Trust

Xenophon walks across his own planet, now covered in cold and evil, He needs to go to destroy Killernet, before he controls the whole planet. I hate Killernet! Xenophon shouted. Suddenly three cyborg lions crashed into Xenophon’s hiding place, he is found by killernet’s tracker cyborgs! He didn’t flinch, as he grabbed his energy laser sword given by the gods as an honor of his fate, he slashed the first cyborg, and grabbed the second one’s tail to knock out the third one out, and at that moment, he WANTS to be the strongest cyborg fighter. Gonna kill HIM, Xenophon whispered.

He flew to a distant village, when the people saw him, they were happy and awed as they saw their hero, Make me a Dragon-Obsidian armor, I need it to defeat our enemy, Killernet, he said, they made for him with care, Xenophon thanked them and flew away in the lonely clouds.

The reason for why Xenophon wants to kill Killernet is because he found out in the village that Killernet murdered his parents and his fellow comrades on purpose just for FUN, he wanted revenge, and traveled for days, just to find the merciless murderer. 

Then suddenly, he was ambushed by a crowd of Killernet Warriors!  Xenophon was slammed to the ground like a rag doll, He roared, Damn! As they were ready to strike again, Xenophon slashed them at their faces with no fear, he stood up, grabbing his sword, You think you can defeat me? Think again. He said it with fury and hate, he easily blowed and killed all of them, then he saw Killernet coming out of his Titanium-made ship, he was wearing dark-iron armor, with big claws sticking out of his back, this was his third form, the last form, and the fight is going to be a bloody one, to death. 

As Killernet lunged in, Xenophon ducked and fired a acid blast, Killernet used his claws to swipe Xenophon, Xenophon leveled up to use more power, both are fighting midair, they seemed like to fought for days, months, and even years. At last, when Killernet shot his final attack, Xenophon threw his laser energy sword and stabbed Killernet in the arm, Killernet tried to run, but suddenly, Xenophon appears behind him, kicked him, and stabbed him in the chest. Now the whole planet is safe, and Xenophon became a Legend Warrior. D-Done… He panted.

All the villagers were shocked that how strong Xenophon is, they trusted and believed that he can be the leader, at last, he was the Emperor Warrior and lived for thousands of years later.

After years of peace, Killernet came to life again, and killed the person who saved him. He was very angry that he was defeated by a low ranking warrior. He burst out flying to find Xenophon for another fight, he know not how mighty strong Xenophon is now. He saw Xenophon, he charged at him, Xenophon blasted his curse right in front of him before Killernet even attacked him, Killernet truly dies, and Xenophon wins a Hero’s glory again.

Xenophon lived perfectly and peacefully for the next few weeks, he thought of his comrades, friends and most importantly, family, they sacrifice so much for me, he thought, he should let this thing go and past, he went to find his only and last family, his sister, Nova Prime.

He can’t stand to die in the next few years, so he made a technology that can turn them living beings into half flesh, half bot body, he successfully survived and the whole village upgraded to immortality


When Xenophon stepped into the village again, wooden doors slammed shut one by one—flickering candlelight seeped through cracks, and trembling whispers tangled in the wind. He paused, fingers brushing the sword hilt. The chill of the night he’d been cast out, calm and serene, pricked his throat… but he let the sword fall to his side.
A child’s face peeked over a windowsill; Xenophon lifted a weathered stone “carved by his father” and set it on the well. “I came to bury the hate,” he called, voice rough but steady. By dawn, he was gone for another adventure—and the village left the stone on the square, a promise to never trade trust for fear. Years later, travelers heard of a village that honored a warrior who chose to protect over surrendering, and a stone that glowed when the wind spoke his name
 
Xenophon…
